Adapted subsystem contracts and implementation paths:

* src/graphics/presentation/window/vulkanWindow.cpp:
  Vulkan instance/device lifetime, physical device/queue selection, physical
  memory properties and shader floating-point capability admission.
* src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h and vulkanCommon.cpp:
  retained device/queue/property ownership and compiled SPIR-V module creation.
* src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/pipeline/pipelineLayoutCache.cpp:
  descriptor set/pipeline layouts and the stage-scoped 128-byte push block.
* src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/pipeline/descriptors.cpp:
  manifest/resource binding number, storage-buffer descriptor count/range and
  actual retained resource ownership.
* src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/pipeline/pipelineCache.cpp:
  compute/graphics pipeline create-info composition and shader-module lifetime.
* src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/commandRecorder.cpp, commandScheduler.cpp,
  masterSemaphore.cpp, renderCompute.cpp and queueSubmission.cpp:
  recording, queue submission, completion ownership and write visibility before
  host readback.
* src/graphics/shader/shaderBindings.h and the separately licensed compiler port:
  explicit original V# specialization, native bindings and shader-data offsets.

PentaX modifications (2026): safe public closed-original factories, checked
opaque compiler outputs/required-feature manifests, bounded Rust host arenas
and dedicated Vulkan allocations, fallible staging/readback buffers, fixed
driver enumeration arrays, private resource borrows and RAII rollback, absolute
Windows system-loader path, a synchronous queue/fence profile, explicit typed
unsupported features, and original AMD compute/vertex/pixel test programs.
Added an opaque prepared-compute entry over the same owned resources, checked
compiler feature/push contracts, actual single-buffer extents, host-supported
dispatch geometry and explicit fenced readback. Core keeps the original guest
owner paused through permission/alias preflight and transactional writeback.
Dedicated memory replaces the source renderer's VMA/cache allocation layer.
No source guest-pointer casting, unbounded caches, global renderer state,
environment-controlled compatibility behavior or guest command parser is ported.
This is a ported subsystem profile, not the complete renderer.

